course: dictionary
lesson: 1557
title: Words that name a doer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words end in -er, and the ending often means a person or thing that does something. A changer is a person or thing that changes something. «The new coin changer gave me smaller coins for my pound.» The machine does the job of changing, so it is a changer.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. «The money-changers sat at their tables in the temple» tells you they were people who swapped one kind of money for another. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: a person who changes money fits.
explain: A changer is often part of a phrase, and the phrase has its own meaning. «Her new idea was a game changer for the whole school.» A game changer is something that changes a situation in a big way, so the phrase means more than its separate words.
fact: A changer is a person or thing that changes something.
fact: A coin changer is a machine that changes things, such as giving you smaller coins for a bigger one.
fact: A game changer is something that changes a situation in a big way.
fact: In 1299 the money-changers of Florence banned the new digits, so people did not always welcome change.
fact: Changer comes from the word change, and the -er ending points to a doer.
exercise: «The new coin changer gave me smaller coins for my pound.» What is a coin changer? | A bank that closes early | *A machine that changes coins into smaller coins | A child who collects coins | A shop that sells only pennies
exercise: «Her new idea was a game changer for the whole school.» What does game changer mean? | A teacher who loves sport | *Something that changes a situation in a big way | A rule that stops all play | A fun new board game
exercise: The word changer ends in -er. What does this ending usually show? | Something that happened in the past | A word that means nothing at all | *A person or thing that does something | A thing that is always broken
test: «The money-changers sat at their tables in the temple.» What were money-changers? | *People who swapped one kind of money for another | Children who played in the courtyard | Guards who kept the gold safe | People who painted the temple walls
test: Which phrase means something that changes a situation in a big way? | coin changer | *game changer | nappy changer | money changer
exam: «The voice changer made my friend sound like a robot.» What is a voice changer? | A person who teaches singing | *A device that changes how a voice sounds | A toy robot that talks | A friend who is always loud
